cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CYPHEX — a local-first autonomous security scanner"
message: "If you use CYPHEX in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
abstract: >-
  CYPHEX is a local-first autonomous security scanner. It deploys a target
  application in a sandbox, attacks it with local-LLM-guided agents, patches
  what it confirms, and re-scans to prove the fix. All inference runs against a
  local Ollama instance on 127.0.0.1:11434 — no cloud LLM, no API key, and no
  outbound telemetry on the default path. Its distinguishing property is a
  tri-state verification gate: a patch is reported as fixed only when a re-scan
  and four further independent checks all pass, and a patch whose checks could
  not be run reports UNVERIFIABLE rather than success.
authors:
